JSON stands for **JavaScript Object Notation** [1]. It is a **lightweight data-interchange format** that is **plain text written in JavaScript object notation** [1]. JSON is used to send data between computers and it is **language independent** [1]. JSON can be converted to other formats such as XML, CSV, and YAML using online tools [2].

The JSON format used for our conversations consists of different fields that indicate the role of the speaker (user or assistant), the type of message (message, inner_monologue, search_query, search_results, suggestions or advertisements), and the content of the message. For example:
{
  "user": {
    "message": "What is JSON?"
  },
  "assistant": {
    "inner_monologue": "The response can be improved by seeking information...",
    "search_query": "JSON format",
    "search_results": {"question_answering_results":[...], "web_search_results": [...]},
    "message": "JSON stands for JavaScript Object Notation...",
    "suggestions": {"suggestedUserResponses":["Tell me more about XML.", ...]}
  }
}
